## DEQUE — LEARNED Mon Mar 30 ✅

```cpp
deque<int> dq;
dq.push_back(x)   // add to back
dq.pop_back()     // remove from back
dq.push_front(x)  // add to front
dq.pop_front()    // remove from front
dq.front()        // peek front
dq.back()         // peek back
dq.empty()        // check if empty
```

**Critical rule:** Always check `!dq.empty()` before accessing `front()` or `back()`.

```cpp
while(!dq.empty() && nums[dq.back()] < nums[r])  // ✅ empty check FIRST
```

